15. bxc3 c5 16. Ne5 Qd5 17. Bxh7+ Kf8 18. Qh5 {Sources: BCM, August 1930, p294.
Given as 'Fairhurst-Seitz' but in BCM, Feb 1950, Dr Seitz had a letter
published saying that he didn't play the game. Fairhurst agreed with him and
it was thought that Black was probably Mortlock. Confirmed by the Glasgow
Herald, 12 July 1930, which also has the game score, clearly marked as
Fairhurst-Mortlock, final round, Major Open 1930, 4 July 1930} 1-0

